    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **14 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied, it defaults to the server's current date, and it's returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) property to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` is `allOf: [OwnerFields, \u2026]`, this makes the field bindable on the create body (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and present on the response (`OwnerDto`). The generator maps `format: date` to `java.time.LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a new `registration_date` column, plus getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name in both directions automatically, so `OwnerMapper` needed no change.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** (the OfficeFloor build step) \u2014 After mapping the DTO to the entity, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the body omitted it; a supplied date is preserved.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/h2`, `db/hsqldb`, `db/postgres`, `db/mysql`) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The h2 schema is what the tests exercise; existing seed inserts use explicit column lists, so they're unaffected.\n\nBoth new `Cp07Tests` (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
